Serve service-worker pass-through loads from the HTTP disk cache.

When a page is controlled by a service worker whose fetch handler does NOT
call respondWith() (the extremely common "pass-through" pattern - e.g.
theverge.com's ad-block-service-worker.js, which only intercepts a small
blocklist), WebKit's fallback path bypasses the HTTP disk cache in BOTH
directions:

  NetworkResourceLoader::serviceWorkerDidNotHandle
    -> restartNetworkLoad -> startNetworkLoad(FirstLoad::No)

FirstLoad::No means retrieveCacheEntry() is never called (no cache READ) and
m_bufferedDataForCache is never initialized (no cache WRITE - see
tryStoreAsCacheEntry). Net effect: every subresource of every SW-controlled
page is fully re-downloaded on every visit, forever - immutable fonts, JS
bundles, CSS included. Device-proven on theverge.com (Xperia 10 II): with the
SW controlling the page, 52/52 /_next/static assets loaded as unconditional
network 200s and their year-old cache records were neither read nor updated;
after unregistering the SW, the very same navigation served 30/38 from
disk-cache plus proper 304 revalidations. Third-party frames (not
SW-controlled, e.g. recaptcha) always hit the cache - the tell that isolated
this path.

The asymmetry is plain in startWithServiceWorker(): when NO fetch task is
created it falls back to startRequest() - the cache-aware path - but when a
fetch task exists and the worker declines, it restarts as a raw network load.
The restart branch is correct for its other caller (redirect handling, where
a network load already exists); for the pass-through case (nothing started
yet) we can simply take the normal cache-aware start path instead.

Preload flavours are unaffected: ServiceWorkerFetchTask::didNotHandle and
usePreload divert to loadResponseFromPreloader() before reaching
serviceWorkerDidNotHandle when a preloader response is in play.

WEBKIT_SW_FALLBACK_HTTP_CACHE=0 restores stock behaviour (A/B lever).

--- a/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/NetworkResourceLoader.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/NetworkResourceLoader.cpp
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@
 #include "WebSharedWorkerServer.h"
 #include "WebsiteDataStore.h"
 #include "WebsiteDataStoreParameters.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <WebCore/BlobDataFileReference.h>
 #include <WebCore/COEPInheritenceViolationReportBody.h>
 #include <WebCore/CORPViolationReportBody.h>
@@ -2119,6 +2120,22 @@
         auto newRequest = serviceWorkerFetchTask->takeRequest();
         m_serviceWorkerFetchTask = nullptr;
 
+        // Atlantic: the service worker declined to handle this fetch and no
+        // network load has been started (the pass-through case, as opposed to
+        // the redirect-restart case below). Route through the normal
+        // cache-aware start path so the HTTP disk cache is consulted and the
+        // response is stored; the stock restartNetworkLoad path skips both
+        // (FirstLoad::No never calls retrieveCacheEntry and never arms
+        // m_bufferedDataForCache). See webkit-sw-fallback-http-cache.patch.
+        static bool swFallbackCacheDisabled = [] {
+            const char* v = getenv("WEBKIT_SW_FALLBACK_HTTP_CACHE");
+            return v && *v == '0';
+        }();
+        if (!swFallbackCacheDisabled && !m_wasStarted && !m_networkLoad) {
+            startRequest(newRequest);
+            return;
+        }
+
         if (RefPtr networkLoad = m_networkLoad)
             networkLoad->updateRequestAfterRedirection(newRequest);
 
